  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gyre B.V.: Developing the Supply Chain for Reusable Bags (Everless Smart Bag) in Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global consumption of single use plastics is over 1,000 billion per year. Despite changing public opinion and legal incentives, the use of single use plastics is still growing and seriously threatening the world, in particular our oceans and sea life.Gyre offers sustainable solutions that are trendy, contemporary and easy to use fashion items. The most important product is the Gyre bag, a reusable and recyclable shopping bag that can replace 300 single use bags.  Gyre wishes to develop a fully sustainable supply chain and manufacturing facility in Vietnam to enable mass (large scale) production. To prepare for future investments, Technical Assistance (DGGF-TA) provided support to develop a supply chain and a technical and financial business plan. The project Included the selection of manufacturing partners,  production development and testing of 300 high quality bags of which the results will be used to determine the technical requirements for production, the development of a CSR production policy according to international standards and the development of a bankable business plan to prepare for future investments in the production facility.The project was successful and supported 30 indirect jobs with Vietnamese local partners and provided knowledge transfer amongst manufacturing partners regarding sustainable production methods. Investments in scale-up activities are being prepared and may lead to additional jobs and less plastic pollution caused by single-use plastic bags.</narrative>
  </description>
